        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9c749008-8cfe-5277-a6cc-815e8ea34c95",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Les Clark, Ub Iwerks, Walt Disney\n- Projects: Mickey Mouse, Oswald the Lucky Rabbit, Plane Crazy\n- Topics: Disney animation, character creation\n\nFacts:\n- In 1927, Les Clark joined Disney.\n- Les Clark was the only person besides Ub Iwerks to work on the origins of Mickey Mouse.\n- Ub Iwerks was born on March 24, 1901, and died on July 7, 1971.\n- Ub Iwerks was an American animator, cartoonist, character designer, inventor, and special effects technician.\n- Ub Iwerks created Oswald the Lucky Rabbit with Walt Disney.\n- Ub Iwerks created Mickey Mouse with Walt Disney.\n- Plane Crazy is an American animated short film.\n- Plane Crazy was directed by Walt Disney and Ub Iwerks.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "32e4fe6c-bf49-5656-b87c-cfa6177f460d",
        "text": "Page: Les Clark. Sentence: Joining Disney in 1927, he was the only one to work on the origins of Mickey Mouse with Ub Iwerks.\nPage: Ub Iwerks. Sentence: Ubbe Eert \"Ub\" Iwerks, A.S.C. ( ; March 24, 1901 – July 7, 1971) was an American animator, cartoonist, character designer, inventor, and special effects technician, who created Oswald the Lucky Rabbit and Mickey Mouse with Walt Disney.\nPage: Plane Crazy. Sentence: Plane Crazy is an American animated short film directed by Walt Disney and Ub Iwerks.",
